{"parentUuid":"f959ca9a-e505-4508-8395-533c6cf395b6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GY8q1rgbhUBZ6UBACjcLbx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have what I need. Let me explain point 3 and give you my review.\n\n## Point 3 explained — \"session matching was strict-equal on `WorktreePath`\"\n\nEvery session record on disk (`.git/entire-sessions/<id>.json`) stores a `WorktreePath` field — captured at session start, from `paths.WorktreeRoot()` at the moment `UserPromptSubmit` fires. When a commit happens, hooks call `findSessionsForWorktree(currentWorktreePath)` to figure out which session(s) should be linked to the commit.\n\nThe lookup was a strict `state.WorktreePath == worktreePath`. With Claude's worktrees feature, the two values diverge:\n\n| moment | who fires what | path observed |\n|---|---|---|\n| user starts Claude in `/repo` | `UserPromptSubmit` from main worktree | session created with `WorktreePath = /repo` |\n| Claude internally spawns a child process inside `/repo/.claude/worktrees/feature-x/` | the child eventually runs `git commit` | git fires `prepare-commit-msg` with CWD = `/repo/.claude/worktrees/feature-x` |\n| hook calls `findSessionsForWorktree(\"/repo/.claude/worktrees/feature-x\")` | strict equal | no match — even though the session exists in main |\n\nWithout a match, the hook logs `no active sessions` at DEBUG and quietly returns. Net effect: no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, no condensation, no metadata push. Issues 1 (`transcript_path` mismatch) and 2 (`.entire/` anchoring) had to be fixed first for the hook to even reach this layer, but on their own they wouldn't have fixed the symptom — point 3 is the last gate.\n\nThe fix in `manual_commit_session.go:150` widens lookup **one-directionally**: when the caller is in a linked worktree, also accept sessions registered against the main worktree. From main, the lookup is unchanged — otherwise a commit on main could accidentally adopt a sibling Claude session running in `.claude/worktrees/<branch>`. Two regression tests cover both directions (`_LinkedWorktreeMatchesMain`, `_MainWorktreeUnchanged`).\n\n## Review of the branch\n\n**Overall: in good shape.** The three fixes match their stated diagnoses, gates are tight, and tests cover both the new code paths and the boundary conditions where the widening must *not* fire.\n\n### Strengths\n\n- **`worktreeParentCandidate`** (`lifecycle.go:262`) — `strings.LastIndex` is the right choice and is explicitly justified in the comment; `TestWorktreeParentCandidate_MarkerInRepoRoot` locks it in. The `idx <= 0` check rejects marker-at-start. Traversal protection via `validation.ValidateAgentSessionID` happens before `filepath.Join`. Candidate must exist before being returned. Permission/IO errors pass through instead of being silently swallowed.\n- **`MainWorktreeRoot`** (`paths.go:151`) — forces `--path-format=absolute` (avoids a relative-path bug class), caches per-cwd like `WorktreeRoot`, and `ClearWorktreeRootCache` clears both caches so test isolation still works.\n- **`AbsPath` split** (`paths.go:202`) — `.entire/*` paths route to main, everything else stays on the linked worktree. `isEntireRelPath` is traversal-resistant. The `TestAbsPath_EntireAnchoredAtMainWorktree` test asserts both halves (main for `.entire/`, linked for `src/`) and the absolute-passthrough.\n- **Widening logic** (`manual_commit_session.go:160-174`) — falls back to strict-equal if `MainWorktreeRoot` resolution fails, so the change can never make any caller worse off than before.\n- **`logging.Init`** (`logger.go`) — fallback chain `MainWorktreeRoot → WorktreeRoot → \".\"` matches expected resilience.\n\n### Things worth flagging\n\n1. **Cross-worktree multi-session coupling.** With the widening in place, a commit in `.claude/worktrees/feature-x` will return *both* the linked-worktree session and the main-worktree session if both exist. `filterSessionsWithNewContent` then checks each session's *own* shadow branch (`getShadowBranchNameForCommit(state.BaseCommit, state.WorktreeID)`, `manual_commit_hooks.go:1565`), so they can't accidentally claim each other's files. But if the main-worktree session has its own real content (e.g., a parallel Claude session that the user is also actively running in `/repo`), both sessions get linked under the same commit. This matches the existing multi-session model (different sessions in the same directory interleave on shadow branches), the PR just extends the boundary across worktrees. Probably fine — but worth double-checking against the `manual_commit.go` multi-session docs to confirm \"different worktrees\" is genuinely intended to behave the same as \"same worktree, different sessions.\"\n\n2. **`MainWorktreeRoot` in submodules.** Inside a submodule, `--git-common-dir` returns the submodule's `.git` dir, not the parent repo's. Parent of that is the submodule root, so `.entire/` resolves to the submodule's `.entire/`. That's almost certainly the correct behavior (submodules are independent entire-state-wise), but it's not stated anywhere and you may want a sentence in the `MainWorktreeRoot` doc clarifying it.\n\n3. **`MainWorktreeRoot` cache invalidation on cwd changes.** Mirrors `WorktreeRoot`'s existing behavior, so consistent — but if any future code path `os.Chdir`s mid-process it'll need to call `ClearWorktreeRootCache`. Existing risk, not introduced here.\n\n4. **Doc nit in `logging.Init` fallback** — \"environments where --git-common-dir resolution fails\" — in practice this also implies `WorktreeRoot` fails (not in a git repo at all), so the secondary fallback to `WorktreeRoot` is dead code. Not worth changing, but the comment slightly overstates the value of the chain.\n\n5. **Upstream Claude limitations** are correctly called out in the PR notes (inner Claude session not firing its own `UserPromptSubmit`, `transcript_path` mismatch). Worth filing those upstream as separate issues, since they're root causes that the fallbacks here paper over.\n\nTests are thorough — unit (`worktreeParentCandidate`, `resolveTranscriptPath` passthrough/empty/no-marker/marker-in-root/marker-at-start/outside-base/traversal/fallback), integration (`TestClaudeCode_WorktreePathFallback`, `TestLinkedWorktree_EntireSetUpVisible`), and the targeted widening tests on both sides. The `TestFindSessionsForWorktree_MainWorktreeUnchanged` test in particular is the right kind of \"this is the cliff, don't step off it\" coverage."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2724,"cache_read_input_tokens":107861,"output_tokens":5730,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2724,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":5730,"cache_read_input_tokens":107861,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2724},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CavwSC3yLuVwnMGuDGhcF","type":"assistant","uuid":"67f14db8-3713-4ac8-b55d-192e780d35b5","timestamp":"2026-05-11T14:29:30.224Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"60f1a956-e1c7-4056-9d0c-a8af3c0315b1","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"fix/claude-worktree-transcript-resolution"}
