{"parentUuid":"9c8c5556-4f1a-4ae7-bf9f-9c9b4f63d0e4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011PSmxGDEGGNtMt1qUqQqRH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right to push back — point #2 in the PR is overstated. The `IsSetUp` gate only checks `settings.json`. In this very repo, `settings.json` is committed (I just confirmed: `git ls-files .entire/` returns `settings.json` and `.gitignore`). So a freshly-added linked worktree gets `.entire/settings.json` checked out just like any other tracked file — and `IsSetUp` returns `true`.\n\nThe PR claim \"**Every** git hook firing from inside a linked worktree saw `IsSetUpAndEnabled = false`\" only holds in narrower cases:\n\n1. **`entire enable --local`-only repos** — only `settings.local.json` exists (which is gitignored, so it never materializes in a linked worktree). `IsSetUp` would fail from main too in that case, *but* `entire status` uses a different gate that checks *both* files (`status.go:86-88`), so status passes in main but not in the linked worktree. That matches the integration test's specific symptom (`TestLinkedWorktree_EntireSetUpVisible`).\n2. **Repos that gitignored `.entire/settings.json` manually.**\n3. **The local file overrides `enabled: true → false` in main**, so main is \"enabled\" but the linked worktree (which can't see `settings.local.json`) reads only the committed value.\n\nThe fix is still load-bearing — but the *real* breakage it cures isn't usually the `IsSetUp` gate. It's:\n\n- `.entire/logs/` is gitignored → hook log writes inside a linked worktree create an orphan `.entire/logs/` inside `.claude/worktrees/<branch>/` instead of writing to the canonical `main/.entire/logs/entire.log`. The PR commit message for `logger.go` calls this out directly: *\"writes to the canonical .entire/logs/entire.log instead of spawning an orphan .entire/logs directory inside each linked worktree.\"*\n- `.entire/settings.local.json` is gitignored