{"parentUuid":"216d37fa-c8af-4716-992f-04de04e46b67","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016cFdCrCQhg5Nw97QQ6xw4H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sharp observation — yes, the `.entire/` split-state problem has affected **every** linked worktree since `git worktree` machinery existed, not just Claude's auto-created ones. Let me lay out exactly what's general vs. what's Claude-specific in this PR:\n\n## What changed in #2 (and who it affects)\n\nThe actual code change in #2 is entirely general — nothing in it knows about Claude:\n\n| What | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `paths.AbsPath(\".entire/...\")` | `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` → current worktree | `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` parent → main worktree |\n| `logging.Init` log dir | current worktree | main worktree |\n\nThis affects **any** linked worktree — `git worktree add ../wt-foo`, jj's colocated worktrees, anything `--git-common-dir` recognizes. A user who manually did `git worktree add ../feat-x && cd ../feat-x && claude` would have hit the same `.entire/logs/` orphaning, the same invisible `settings.local.json` overrides, the same split metadata — and now they don't.\n\n## What *was* broken in manual worktrees before the PR\n\nFor repos with `.entire/settings.json` committed (the common case):\n\n- `IsSetUp` returned `true` from the manual worktree — hooks ran.\n- But log writes went to `wt-foo/.entire/logs/` (gitignored, orphaned, not where you'd `tail -f`).\n- `.entire/settings.local.json` was invisible — any user-local override (log_level=DEBUG, custom settings) was silently ignored.\n- Transient state under `.entire/tmp/`, `.entire/metadata/` split between trees.\n- This had been broken forever; nobody hit it as a *visible* breakage because nobody routinely commits agent work from a manually-created worktree.\n\nFor `entire enable --local`-only repos:\n- `IsSetUp` returned `false` from the manual worktree too — `entire status` and the hook gate both saw \"not set up.\" Also broken forever; equally invisible because nobody used both flags together.\n\n## What *is* genuinely new in this PR\n\n- **#1 (transcript path) is Claude-specific.** That's a bug in Claude Code itself — `transcript_path` is encoded from the worktree CWD but the file is written to the parent project dir. Doesn't affect any other agent or any manual workflow.\n- **#3 (session matching widening) is Claude-specific.** It only matters when the *session* was created in one worktree (main) and the *commit* fires from a different one (the linked worktree the agent spawned). Manual `git worktree add ../wt-foo && cd ../wt-foo && claude` doesn't hit this — UserPromptSubmit fires from `wt-foo`, the commit fires from `wt-foo`, strict equality matches. The bug requires an agent that spawns a subprocess into a different worktree while keeping the parent session alive. Today, that's Claude's worktrees feature.\n- **#2 is general.** Claude's worktrees feature was the *trigger* that made the long-standing bug visible (auto-creates linked worktrees, auto-commits from inside them), but the fix happens to repair manual worktrees for free.\n\n## What the PR description gets a bit wrong\n\nThe framing — \"Three independent issues conspired to make agent work in linked worktrees invisible to Entire\" — bundles a general linked-worktree fix (#2) into a Claude-narrative as though it were specific to Claude. It would be more accurate to say:\n\n> #2 is a pre-existing bug in linked-worktree support that we're fixing now because Claude's worktrees feature finally made it visible. #1 and #3 are Claude-specific.\n\nThat framing would also nudge a follow-up question worth asking: are there other places that resolve relative paths from CWD-based git roots and should switch to `MainWorktreeRoot` for `.entire/*`? The PR fixed `paths.AbsPath` and `logging.Init` — anything that does `os.ReadFile(\".entire/...\")` directly without going through `AbsPath` is still broken in any linked worktree."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2048,"cache_read_input_tokens":136859,"output_tokens":3421,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2048,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3421,"cache_read_input_tokens":136859,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2048,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2048},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CavxtXbJiajL23JJpBq9S","type":"assistant","uuid":"7a3220c2-eff3-4b2d-a744-9413acf41496","timestamp":"2026-05-11T14:48:09.964Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"60f1a956-e1c7-4056-9d0c-a8af3c0315b1","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"fix/claude-worktree-transcript-resolution"}
