{"parentUuid":"dea8a7a2-f43c-453c-bcea-581d63a40211","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BdEJRwkfxD8kAKYYwQNomJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — and I think it's actually a strictly better design. Here's the logic:\n\n## The proposed lookup\n\n```go\nfunc (s *ManualCommitStrategy) findSessionsForWorktree(ctx context.Context, worktreePath string) ([]*SessionState, error) {\n    allStates, err := s.listAllSessionStates(ctx)\n    if err != nil { return nil, err }\n\n    var localMatches []*SessionState\n    for _, state := range allStates {\n        if state.WorktreePath == worktreePath {\n            localMatches = append(localMatches, state)\n        }\n    }\n    if len(localMatches) > 0 {\n        return localMatches, nil\n    }\n\n    // No local match. If we're in a linked worktree, fall back to main.\n    mainPath, mainErr := paths.MainWorktreeRoot(ctx)\n    if mainErr != nil || mainPath == \"\" || mainPath == worktreePath {\n        return nil, nil\n    }\n    var mainMatches []*SessionState\n    for _, state := range allStates {\n        if state.WorktreePath == mainPath {\n            mainMatches = append(mainMatches, state)\n        }\n    }\n    return mainMatches, nil\n}\n```\n\n## Why this is better\n\nWalk through the scenarios:\n\n| scenario | current PR | middle-ground |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A. Claude's worktrees feature** (outer session in main, child commits from linked) | linked finds nothing → widens to main → links outer session ✓ | linked finds nothing → falls back to main → links outer session ✓ |\n| **B. User does `git worktree add ../wt-foo && cd ../wt-foo && claude`** (independent session created in wt-foo) | linked finds wt-foo session, ALSO widens to include any main session in the bundle ✗ | linked finds wt-foo session, stops — main session is NOT bundled ✓ |\n| **C. Concurrent: separate Claude in main AND in wt-foo** (both legitimately working independently) | wt-